%I A402150 #9 Nov 27 2026 16:53:41
%S A402150 1,1,1,1,1,2,1,1,3,3,1,3,1,4,6,1,1,8,1,6,10,5,1,4,10,6,15,10,1,20,1,1,
%T A402150 15,7,20,15,1,8,21,10,1,40,1,15,45,9,1,5,35,45,28,21,1,48,35,20,36,10,
%U A402150 1,45,1,11,105,1,56,70,1,28,45,105,1,24,1,12,126
%N A402150 Number of 1-based restricted growth permutations of row n of A305936 (a multiset whose multiplicities are the prime indices of n).
%C A402150 This described multiset (row n of A305936, Heinz number A181821) is generally not the same as the multiset of prime indices of n (A112798). For example, the prime indices of 12 are {1,1,2}, while a multiset whose multiplicities are {1,1,2} is {1,1,2,3}.
%C A402150 A prime index of n is a number m such that prime(m) divides n. The multiset of prime indices of n is row n of A112798, sum A056239.
%C A402150 A 1-based restricted growth sequence of length j is a sequence (a_1, ..., a_j), satisfying a_1 = 1 and a_i <= 1 + max(a_1, ..., a_{i-1}) for all i = 2, 3, ..., j. We also include the empty sequence.
%C A402150 Note that although this sequence covers the positive integers, after a(15) = 6 it is not itself a 1-based restricted growth sequence.
%C A402150 Positions of terms > 1 are given by A111774.
%F A402150 A402149(n) + A402150(n) = A318762(n).
%e A402150 The a(12) = 3 permutations are: (1123), (1213), (1231), not including (1132), (1312), (1321), (2113), (2131), (2311), (3112), (3121), (3211).
%t A402150 nrmptn[n_]:=Join@@MapIndexed[Table[#2[[1]],{#1}]&,If[n==1,{},Flatten[Cases[FactorInteger[n]//Reverse,{p_,k_}:>Table[PrimePi[p],{k}]]]]];
%t A402150 rgoQ[y_]:=y=={}||y[[1]]==1&&And@@Table[y[[i]]<=1+Max@@Take[y,i-1],{i,2,Length[y]}];
%t A402150 Table[Length[Select[Permutations[nrmptn[n]],rgoQ]],{n,100}]
%Y A402150 For normal sequences see A000110, complement A402144.
%Y A402150 Positions of terms > 1 are A111774.
%Y A402150 Positions of 1 are A174090.
%Y A402150 Without restricted growth we have A318762.
%Y A402150 For prime indices we have A402146, complement A402147.
%Y A402150 The complement is counted by A402149.
%Y A402150 A008480 counts permutations of prime indices.
%Y A402150 A383253 counts restricted growth compositions, ranks A402139, triangle A383713.
%Y A402150 A402138 counts non-restricted growth compositions, ranks A402141, triangle A402142.
%Y A402150 A402140 counts covering compositions without restricted growth, ranks A402143.
%Y A402150 Cf. A001221, A001222, A005651, A007716, A055932, A181821, A305936, A318283, A318360, A401975, A402151, A402152.
